; B2b conformance oracle: does the effect core satisfy the real lwt.mli?
;
; [candidate_lwt.mli] is an UNCHANGED copy of [src/core/lwt.mli]; [candidate_lwt.ml]
; backs it with the effect core. Building this library therefore reports the exact
; conformance gap (missing names, then type/shape mismatches) that the in-place
; core swap (B2b) must close — and, once green, that the candidate IS a drop-in.
;
; Disabled by default so the branch stays buildable: flip [enabled_if] to [true]
; (or `dune build @test/oracle/all`) to re-measure while doing conformance work.
(library
 (name candidate_lwt)
 (enabled_if false)
 (flags (:standard -alert -all))
 (libraries lwt_effects))
